{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms","id":1150020,"title":"The Fallen Realms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-15T15:51:25-07:00","id":1150020,"title":"The Fallen Realms","content":"This is something that I`ve wanted to do for a loooong time. The moment I heard that a book on the Fallen Realms is being written, or will be written I got inspired to do this...<br /> <br /> So, without further ado, can we list all places, worlds and realms mentioned in the books? Like a list of all those places where Awakened end up occasionally in their pursuit of mysteries and obsessions?<br /> <br /> So, fill in the gaps if I forgot any realm and feel free to correct if I made any mistakes.<br /> <br /> First we have Material/Earth/Flesh/our world. Then there is Twilight/Nether Khertet. Then we have Gauntlet, and mentioned in the Free Council book, a misty realm within Gauntlet. Then there is Shadow Realm/Hisil with all it's weirdness like places that do not correspond to real flesh locations and Wounds.<br /> We also have the Underworld with a lot of locations and Dead Dominions.<br /> We have Astral with it's layers: Oneiros, Temenos, Anima Mundi and Primordial Dream... <br /> We also have Hedge and Fae Arcadia (which is not Supernal, not to be confused)<br /> Then weirder things come to mind...<br /> I think that in one of the mage books in 1e there is a place that's jamming the Underworld so Souls go to that place instead. I think it's in the Boston book or Supernal Tarot, but I could easily be mistaken.<br /> Then there are various Emanation Realms from both 1e and 2e.<br /> Sta-au from VtR access some weird realm but it could be Twilight.<br /> Then we have Lower Depths. Abbadon/Inferno, Dis, Gardens of Cwn Annwen and Duat. <br /> I don`t know should I mention Aaru cause it could be Supernal. I like to believe that its not.<br /> Then we have Empyrean that could also be either above Supernal or in Lower Depths ( or both just to mess up with cosmology theories )<br /> In the end we have a Place Between where Exarch of Abyss, The Gate, is said to reside.<br /> We have Abyss and Supernal...<br /> So... did I miss anything or is it all that is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T15:54:57-07:00","id":1150021,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s been one or two references to somehow going into a realm inside the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T16:08:20-07:00","id":1150023,"title":"","content":"Yes, you\u2019re missing plenty of realm references.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T16:29:49-07:00","id":1150029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150021#post1150021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s been one or two references to somehow going into a realm inside the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, the realm within the Gauntlet <i>is</i> mentioned. Though it would be more accurate to say that the Gauntlet is a realm rather than containing a realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150023#post1150023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you\u2019re missing plenty of realm references.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind helping filling in the gaps?<br /> <br /> Here's a few corrections and suggestions:<br /> \u200bTwilight is a state of being rather than a realm. If it were, you'd have to list at least four different kinds of Twilight since they don't intersect. (Ghosts, spirits, GM-angels, and goetia.)<br /> The Gauntlet was previously the Border Marches/Pangaea, and looked quite differently back then. Just a note.<br /> The Primordial Dream is located within the Temenos rather than being a separate part of the Astral.<br /> The first, oft ignored, layer of the Astral are the dream spaces (i.e. regular dreams), before the Oneiroi, the Temenos and the Anima Mundi.<br /> The Land of the Worms that Sta-Au has claimed as their territory is actually just badlands on the North American continent.<br /> Mages with Space 5 can create pocket dimensions. Spaces that are not connected to the material, but still accessible through Sympathy like all the Fallen Realms.<br /> Arch-mages I believe creates Chantries within their souls that can turn into Wendings. I might be wrong, though. I'm not that familiar with that part of the Mage cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-15-2017, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T18:44:17-07:00","id":1150047,"title":"","content":"Notably, Mummy treats Twilight as a place, rather than a state of being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T21:41:19-07:00","id":1150065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150023#post1150023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you\u2019re missing plenty of realm references.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the specific locations in each realm? That could be hard. I think the point of some places like the lower depths and temenos realms is that there are so damn many of them that listing them is impossible. So GM have a lot of freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T22:34:26-07:00","id":1150078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150047#post1150047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notably, Mummy treats Twilight as a place, rather than a state of being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also put it in the list cause of Mummy. Not to mention those two mountains in the distance that everyone can see and no-one can reach...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T22:38:15-07:00","id":1150080,"title":"","content":"I also forgot the Plains of Bones and the peyote realm from Mummy the Curse. First one is connected to an artifact and the second is from Rio and connected to an Amkhat... again, correct me if I'm wrong","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T23:56:41-07:00","id":1150092,"title":"","content":"The Core Mummy Book describes one of the Lower Depths, wait was that the Plain of Bones?<br /> <br /> Aaru is the Supernal, hence the Scroll of Ages.<br /> <br /> Arcadia is not necessarily two separate places, Hedge could be the Fallen Reflection. After all in Arcadia you learn to make contracts with Platonic Ideals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T00:38:16-07:00","id":1150096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150092#post1150092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcadia is not necessarily two separate places, Hedge could be the Fallen Reflection. After all in Arcadia you learn to make contracts with Platonic Ideals.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been repeatedly stated by devs that it is two separate places with no relation beyond name and both having ties to a form of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T02:18:29-07:00","id":1150101,"title":"","content":"Aaru is Supernal from the mummy's point of view, not mage`s... I think someone, maybe even devs, said that it's not necessarily Supernal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T02:35:17-07:00","id":1150104,"title":"","content":"Hunter has interstitial terrains, including whatever outer realm was glimpsed in the Ten Photographs of Philadelphia story from the Horror Recognition Guide.<br /> The God-Machine's deeper facilities and more complicated workings are generally technically part of the material realm, but segregated and temporally folded in ways that resemble pocket dimensions and alternate timelines.<br /> Summoners has a chapter on things from other, uncategorized realms, such as the inhuman and transitory Men in Black and the world-parasite Hellmenth (which are probably the soul-siphons you recall from first edition).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T07:11:58-07:00","id":1150132,"title":"","content":"I don't know why, but I think that Hellmenth come from Lower Depths. Not sure if I read it somewhere or not...<br /> Quincux or something similar, not sure on pronunciation, also come from some weird realm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T08:20:51-07:00","id":1150145,"title":"","content":"Other, hard to categorize realms fits the description of lower depths pretty well in any case. Not saying all of them are lower realms, but some could be. I just read the entry on them in summoners and it does not say their realm is a lower depth, merely that it is &quot;below the underworld&quot; (like, you know, lower depths).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T14:44:48-07:00","id":1150210,"title":"","content":"One thing I just remembered right now... Cheiron's board of directors is consisted of... aliens? Entities? That came from another world/Earth because their world was destroyed... so we have that world too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T15:01:12-07:00","id":1150217,"title":"","content":"The home of the Strix is probably some form of lower depth within mage terminology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T15:21:48-07:00","id":1150218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150217#post1150217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The home of the Strix is probably some form of lower depth within mage terminology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I just named it Dis when I mentioned it with Lower Depths... Birds of Dis, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T16:01:45-07:00","id":1150226,"title":"","content":"<i>Summoners</i> also mentions a place of pure Matter, whence come those weird planes that bestow gifts on those who perform the proper sacrifice.<br /> <br /> Seattle has timeline splinters, which could easily exist elsewhere as well.<br /> <br /> You could potentially count the Skein as another realm too, though that's more of a case of changelings and mages interacting with the dreaming world in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T16:51:27-07:00","id":1150234,"title":"","content":"The Skein does not fit in with the mages' model of the Astral. It might be a fifth Astral Realm, though. I believe DaveB has suggested (which is not the same as claiming) that the Skein could be for Dreamspace and Oneiroi what the Gauntlet is for Flesh and Shadow. Werewolves simply pass right through the Gauntlet but mages can visit it as a realm. Mages simply pass right through the barrier between dreams and the Astral proper, but perhaps changelings can visit it as a realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T02:26:36-07:00","id":1150290,"title":"","content":"Where do Morpheans come from? Astral or Arcadia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T04:08:46-07:00","id":1150297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150290#post1150290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do Morpheans come from? Astral or Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don\u2019t come from the Astral, they reside there as a function of their lichdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T04:56:17-07:00","id":1150299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150297#post1150297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don\u2019t come from the Astral, they reside there as a function of their lichdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely remember Morpheans being something else in Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:46:36-07:00","id":1150324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150299#post1150299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vaguely remember Morpheans being something else in Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're godlike dream-entities encountered in the Skein; all three of the examples Dancers in the Dusk gives are explicitly or implicitly cast as separate beings from the True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:47:47-07:00","id":1150326,"title":"","content":"There's also two kind of Morpheans in mage, the astral liches allready mentioned and a kind of astral entity that comes from the oneiros of a person (details are in Summoners)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T14:49:42-07:00","id":1150471,"title":"","content":"One more question. I had an idea about a realm/world similar to Ravenloft + world from Dark Souls + CofD... where would you locate a place like that in Telurian? My guess is Lower Depths, but that begs a question of what does a realm like that lack, since almost every realm in Lower Depths is missing something that it desperately needs to obtain/eat/devour","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T14:53:37-07:00","id":1150472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150471#post1150471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more question. I had an idea about a realm/world similar to Ravenloft + world from Dark Souls + CofD... where would you locate a place like that in Telurian? My guess is Lower Depths, but that begs a question of what does a realm like that lack, since almost every realm in Lower Depths is missing something that it desperately needs to obtain/eat/devour</div> </div> </div> </div>Life? Most of the people of Ravenloft were taken from another world, right? It could lack basically anything that relies on humanity. If you want to get specific you might go for tragedy, dread, or angst, though. Everyone there is tortured or afraid.<br /> <br /> Of course you have a place for such a thing to already exist, in Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-17-2017, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T15:07:29-07:00","id":1150477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150471#post1150471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more question. I had an idea about a realm/world similar to Ravenloft + world from Dark Souls + CofD... where would you locate a place like that in Telurian? My guess is Lower Depths, but that begs a question of what does a realm like that lack, since almost every realm in Lower Depths is missing something that it desperately needs to obtain/eat/devour</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just make that a mystery and decide later. I plan on putting a Narnia/Filliory analogue in my setting that mages will find and be able to get to but I've not tied it to any known realm yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T05:44:11-07:00","id":1150613,"title":"","content":"Hi there. Is this M:tA 1ed Map of the Cosmos still okay. Or are there adjustments to make?<br /> <a href=\"https://4.bp.blogspot.com/-5CXnYoPJTAg/VoA5N-eoNsI/AAAAAAAAi90/Vsy0CeHrtds/s1600/Tellurian_zps75f8422f.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">1. Map:</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://img13.deviantart.net/8151/i/2012/174/6/d/new_world_of_darkness_cosmology_map_drawing_by_willworks-d54kdaf.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">2. Map:</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T05:52:52-07:00","id":1150617,"title":"","content":"Neither of them were accurate in 1e either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T10:15:36-07:00","id":1150681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1150020-the-fallen-realms?p=1150613#post1150613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there. Is this M:tA 1ed Map of the Cosmos still okay. Or are there adjustments to make?<br /> <a href=\"https://4.bp.blogspot.com/-5CXnYoPJTAg/VoA5N-eoNsI/AAAAAAAAi90/Vsy0CeHrtds/s1600/Tellurian_zps75f8422f.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">1. Map:</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://img13.deviantart.net/8151/i/2012/174/6/d/new_world_of_darkness_cosmology_map_drawing_by_willworks-d54kdaf.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">2. Map:</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Due to the (delightfully) sandboxy nature of the NWod, I doubt we will ever be able to make these 'accurate' per say. Too many questions exist about exactly what is what, with the answers shrouded in murky mystery, the Truth known only by fickle, potent gods of trickery and creation (IE, the average Mage Storyteller).<br /> <br /> I would submit though that both maps can be said to be &quot;Okay&quot; for use in play though, since they do a decent job of visualising the core aspects of the cosmology in a clever, eye catching way. I actually had not seen that pencil drawn one before, thank you for sharing it (I currently use the other in my Roll20 game). Both would work great as in universe documents players could discover, perhaps each lays out the particular perspectives of a different clan of planehopping explorers, who meet up to have bitter debates about the exact relationship between Yggdrasil and the Primal Wyld.<br /> <br /> On a 'nitpicky' note, I'm not sure about how map 1 displays Emanation realms. My understanding is that many different ones exist, and the ones displayed here are just examples, but the map makes it look like only 5 exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","user":"Katana1515","date":". 10-18-2017, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T10:37:42-07:00","id":1150693,"title":"","content":"First map is mine... glad someone is using it still.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But even back when I drawn it, it was meant to be a prop and not completely accurate. It was there to show my players what else is out there, beyond our world...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T14:23:20-07:00","id":1150778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted 